  "description": "8-channel bidirectional voltage-level translator with automatic direction sensing - no direction-control pin. It bridges a lower-voltage A-side (1.4-3.6 V) to a higher-voltage B-side (1.65-5.5 V) and tolerates open-drain signals, so it works on push-pull buses (SPI, generic GPIO) and, with care, on I2C. An output-enable (OE) pin puts all I/Os in high-impedance. The common 8-channel module for mixing 3.3 V and 5 V logic.",
