  "typical_application": "Translate 8 logic lines between a 3.3 V and a 5 V (or other mixed) domain - SPI, GPIO, and I2C - with automatic direction and no DIR pin.",
  "gotchas": [
    "VCCA must be <= VCCB; swapping the low- and high-voltage sides breaks translation",
    "OE must be low at power-up and brought high after both rails are valid, or outputs can glitch",
    "it has internal pull-ups (one-shot edge accelerators); on an I2C bus these add to the bus loading and can fight strong external pull-ups - the simpler BSS138 FET shifter is often preferred for I2C",
    "unlike the TXB0108, the TXS0108E tolerates open-drain/I2C, but only at lower data rates (~1.2 Mbps)",
    "auto-direction needs the driving side to overcome the internal pull-up; very weak/high-impedance sources can confuse direction sensing"
  ],
